title: Agent-facing usage guide
desc:19
pidly agents writes a section into AGENTS.md, or whichever of CLAUDE.md,
GEMINI.md or .cursorrules the project already has, between HTML comment
markers so re-running replaces it in place and leaves surrounding text alone.

The section leads with the format rather than the CLI, because it has to work
for an agent in a checkout where pidly was never installed. Commands are the
convenient path, find/sed/mv the guaranteed one. It stays short: it is
injected into every agent's context.

The needs on this ticket originally named 2, the whole script. That was
wrong — the guide depends on the format being settled and on claim existing,
not on every subcommand — so it was narrowed to 3.

Done: implemented in bin/pidly, covered by tests/agents.sh (17 cases).
Follow-on in 9: check should notice when an installed block has gone stale.
